@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Quizzy Moderator Release - Design Notes
+
+## Architecture
+- Rust + Axum 0.8 + Tokio + rusqlite (system SQLite, no bundled build for speed)
+- Single binary `quizzy`, single file `src/main.rs` (~1300 lines)
+- Per-request SQLite connections to `storage/quizzy.sqlite` with WAL + foreign_keys
+- Stateless preview via URL query params (`q`, `score`, `picked`), no session storage
+- Basic auth middleware for all `/moderate*` (401 + WWW-Authenticate on fail)
+- Static assets embedded via `include_str!/include_bytes!` served at `/assets/*`
+
+## Data Model
+- `quizzes(id, title)`
+- `questions(id, quiz_id, body, active, position)` ordered by position
+- `options(id, question_id, body, is_correct, position)` ordered by position
+- Move up/down swaps `position` with neighbor; gaps tolerated
+
+## Key Behaviors
+- Quiz form: Title required (HTML + server), Save redirects to quiz page
+- Question form: 4 empty rows for new; JS `Add option` appends `Option N` + `Option N is correct` with correct `for`/`id`/`name` (`option_text_N`, `option_correct_N`); empty trimmed rows skipped; needs >=2 and >=1 correct; on fail re-render with raw typed rows + errors, no DB write
+- Quiz page: `ul.question-list > li` per question, active numbered 1..N, inactive `—` + dimmed; Move buttons always enabled (no-op at ends); Active checkbox `onchange=submit` with hidden `_form` to detect unchecked; Edit link; Delete with `confirm()`
+- Preview: only active in order; `GET /preview` -> `?q=0&score=0`; options as `POST /preview/answer` buttons; PRG to `?q&score&picked`; Correct!/Wrong! + `is-correct` reveal; Next/See score; `Score: X/N`; Start over single link per page to avoid Capybara ambiguity
+- Lists: `ul.quiz-list > li` and `ul.question-list > li` with buttons inside li for QA scoping
+
+## Offline
+- `cargo vendor` + `.cargo/config.toml` source replacement ensures `cargo build --release --offline` works without registry cache
+- `bin/serve` does `mkdir -p storage`, offline release build, exec; binds 0.0.0.0:$PORT, plain HTTP, any Host
+
+## Design
+- Reuses `docs/mockups/quizzy.css` + font as `assets/*`; admin layout matches mockups (header, page-head, cards, pill buttons); preview uses `.play` phone styles + `.preview-banner`
+
+## Export / Import (2026-10-07)
+- Routes: `GET /moderate/quizzes/{id}/export` (single `<pre>` with pretty JSON), `GET+POST /moderate/quizzes/import` (canonical) + alias `GET+POST /moderate/import`; both behind Basic-auth middleware via `/moderate*` prefix
+- Links: quiz page head adds `<a>Export</a>` next to Preview; `/moderate` head adds `<a>Import quiz</a>` next to New quiz
+- Import form: `<label for="quiz_json">Quiz JSON</label><textarea id="quiz_json" name="quiz_json">` + `<button>Import</button>`; preserves input on error; form posts to canonical import URL
+- Export structs (`ExportQuiz/Question/Option` with `Serialize`) guarantee exactly `title/questions/text/active/options/text/correct` keys in example order; `to_string_pretty` (2-space) + `html_escape` for `<pre>` (only `<pre>` on page)
+- Import validation via `serde_json::Value` + manual checks (no panics on wrong types): blank→`Title can't be blank`, missing/non-array questions→`Questions must be a list`, per-question `Question N: Question can't be blank` / `Add at least two options` / `Mark at least one option as correct` / `Invalid active|correct value` / `Option text can't be blank`; blank option strings skipped like form, missing/non-string text is error; `active` defaults true, `correct` defaults false, extra keys ignored
+- Atomic: validate all in memory first, then `BEGIN` transaction inserting quiz + questions (pos 1..N) + options (pos 0..) preserving JSON order; `tx.commit` or rollback; success `303` to `/moderate/quizzes/{new_id}` (always new row, duplicate titles allowed)
+- Deps: added direct `serde_json = "1.0.151"` (already vendored via axum); `cargo build --release --offline` still works, `Cargo.lock` updated with direct edge; no new vendor needed
+
+## Live Game (2026-10-07)
+- Tables: `games(id, quiz_id, code UNIQUE 5-char, status lobby/open/closed/finished, current_question_id)`, `players(id, game_id, name, token UNIQUE 32-hex)`, `answers(id, game_id, player_id, question_id, option_id, UNIQUE(player_id, question_id))` with WAL + busy_timeout 5s for crowded Wi-Fi concurrency
+- Codes: `ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZ23456789` (no I,O,0,1) via `/dev/urandom` + xorshift fallback; tokens 16 random bytes hex; QR via `qrcode 0.14` `svg` only (no `image` dep, tiny offline build)
+- Routes: `POST /moderate/quizzes/{id}/games` (Start a game form) → `GET /moderate/games/{code}` big screen + `GET .../state` JSON + `POST .../start|finish|next|end`; player `GET /play/{code}` + `GET .../state` + `POST .../join|answer` (urlencoded + JSON, cookie/query/header token)
+- Moderator auth: Basic + `quizzy_mod` HttpOnly session cookie (in-memory HashSet, set on Basic success) so `fetch()` polling works; fixes Chromium `fetch` with `user:pass@host` base URL error by using `ORIGIN = protocol+//+host` absolute URLs (relative fetch fails with "Request cannot be constructed from URL that includes credentials", XHR works)
+- Big screen: lobby shows title, `host/play/CODE` plain text (no scheme, Host header), inline QR SVG same string, `Players: N`, Start; open shows `Question X of N`, body, `ol.stage-options>li`, `Answers: X / Y`, Finish; closed adds per-option `stage-option__count` + `Correct` mark + bars, Next/End quiz; finished `The quiz is over`; all server-rendered + JS `setInterval 500ms` re-render preserving QR (not in JSON for Wi-Fi), actions via `fetch POST` + immediate state
+- Player: join form `Your name` label+placeholder + Join; `Hi, name!` waiting; open `button.play-option` + `Your answer` mark, upsert last pick; closed `Correct!/Wrong!/No answer` via server `result_text/class` (JS has no Correct/Wrong strings, JSON omits `is_correct` before closed, page source clean); finished `The quiz is over`; remember via `quizzy_CODE` cookie + `localStorage quizzy_player_CODE`, state checks cookie/query/header; can join lobby/open/closed, not finished
+- Live: polling 500ms, small JSON, ignore fetch errors for crowded Wi-Fi, change-detection to avoid flicker/input loss; all labels exact, lists in li, confirm() for deletes only
+- Offline: `qrcode` vendored (`cargo vendor` after temp-disable config), `cargo build --release --offline` ~4s, `include_str!` for `big_screen.js`/`play.js` (inlined, no extra requests)
+
+## Prizes / Scoring / Winners (2026-10-07)
+- Schema: `quizzes.num_winners INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 3`, `games.question_opened_at INTEGER (ms)`, `answers.answered_at/elapsed_ms INTEGER (ms)`, `game_winners(game_id,player_id PK)`; `init_db` creates fresh + migrates old via `PRAGMA table_info` + `ALTER TABLE`, backfills `num_winners=3` where NULL/<1, no new crates so offline build unchanged
+- Settings: `GET /moderate/quizzes/{id}/settings` adds `<label for="num_winners">Number of winners</label><input type=number min=1 required>` with current value (3 default); `POST /moderate/quizzes/{id}` validates title + `num_winners>=1` (supports `num_winners|number_of_winners|winners`), errors `Title can't be blank` / `Number of winners must be at least 1` re-rendered via `render_settings_form` preserving input, no DB write on fail; `POST /moderate/quizzes` (new) defaults 3, validates if field present
+- Timing: `now_ms()` = `SystemTime::now` millis; `do_start/do_next` set `question_opened_at=now_ms()` (fallback if column missing); `POST /play/{code}/answer` computes `elapsed=max(0,now-opened)` (0 if NULL) and upserts `answered_at/elapsed_ms` so last pick wins; per-request connections with WAL+busy_timeout handle concurrency
+- Scoring: `compute_scores(game)` = per player `COUNT correct` + `SUM(elapsed)` for correct only (`JOIN options is_correct=1`, NULL→0), sorted `points desc, total_time asc, name.lower asc, id asc`, place=index+1; `points_text` = `1 point` vs `N points`; `PlayState` omits `place/points/*` (`skip_serializing_if None`) before finished so phones see no points during game, `ModGameState.leaderboard` empty before finished
+- Live speed: polling `POLL_MS 250ms` (was 500ms) for both `big_screen.js`/`play.js`, small JSON, ignore fetch errors; server `opened_at` ensures fairness, all clients see question within ~250ms of moderator POST (which also `fetchState()` immediately)
+- Finished big screen: `build_mod_state` for `finished` builds `leaderboard: Vec<LeaderEntry{place,player_id,name,points,points_text,total_time_ms,is_winner}>` + `winners: Vec<id>` + `num_winners`; `render_big_screen_inner` shows `The quiz is over` + `<ol class=leaderboard id=leaderboard><li class="leader[ is-winner]"><span leader__place>1</span><span leader__name>Alice</span><span leader__score>2 points</span>[<span mark--winner>Winner</span>]` in order + controls `<button id=btn-top>Top N</button><button id=btn-draw>Draw</button><button id=btn-reset>Reset winners</button>`; JS `render(finished)` uses `JSON.stringify` sig to avoid flicker/button loss, re-binds `POST .../top|draw|reset-winners`
+- Finished phones: `build_play_state` for `finished+joined` finds player in `compute_scores` → `place/total_players/place_text="Place X of Y"/points/points_text/is_winner`; `render_player_inner` shows `The quiz is over` + `<div id=place>Place X of Y</div><div id=points>N points</div>` + `<div id=won class=winner-banner>You won!` if winner; JS `render(finished)` change-detects `place_text/points_text/is_winner` for live winners without flicker; not-joined after finished sees only `The quiz is over`
+- Winners routes: `POST /moderate/games/{code}/top|draw|reset-winners` (+ aliases `/winners/top|draw|reset`) behind Basic middleware, only when `finished`, else return state; `set_winners` = `DELETE+INSERT OR IGNORE`; JSON response = fresh `ModGameState`, HTML fallback = redirect to big screen
+- Winners logic: `compute_top_winner_ids` = first N of leaderboard filtered `points>0`; `compute_draw_winner_ids` = if `scored<=N` all scored, else `cutoff=scores[N-1].points` (>0), `winners=points>cutoff`, `remaining=N-winners.len()`, `candidates=points==cutoff` shuffled via `random_shuffle` (Fisher-Yates with `game_random_bytes`) truncated to `remaining`; zeros never win, speed ignored for Draw, each Draw re-shuffles; `N=quiz_num_winners()` (max(1,3 default))
+- QA labels: exact visible `Number of winners`, `Top 3`, `Draw`, `Reset winners`, `Winner`, `You won!`, `2 points/1 point/0 points`, `Place 2 of 5`, `End quiz`; leaderboard `ol>li` each with place+name+points, phones `Place`+`points` live via polling
+
+## Timer (2026-10-07)
+- Schema: `quizzes.timer_minutes/timer_seconds INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0`; `init_db` creates fresh + migrates old via `PRAGMA table_info` + `ALTER TABLE`, backfills negatives/NULL to 0; no new crates so `cargo build --release --offline` ~4s unchanged
+- Settings: `GET /moderate/quizzes/{id}/settings` adds `<label for="timer_minutes">Timer minutes</label><input type=number min=0>` + same for seconds with current values (0 default); `POST /moderate/quizzes/{id}` validates `>=0` (supports `timer_minutes|timer-minutes|timerMinutes` etc., blank→0), errors `Timer minutes/seconds must be 0 or more` re-rendered via `render_settings_form` preserving input, no DB write on fail; `POST /moderate/quizzes` (new) defaults 0/0, validates if present; total=`m*60+s`, 0 means no timer
+- Helpers: `quiz_timer_total_seconds()` (clamped), `format_timer()` M:SS (`1:30`,`0:05`,`0:00` via `ceil(remaining/1000)`), `timer_remaining_ms/text()` from `question_opened_at+total-now`; `is_timer_expired()` + `maybe_auto_finish()` (UPDATE to `closed` where `status=open` if `now>=expires`, sets `opened_at=now` if NULL for old games)
+- State: `ModGameState` adds `timer_seconds` (total) + `remaining_ms/text/opened_at` (`None` unless `open`+timer>0, `remaining_ms` clamped `max(0)`); `build_mod_state` computes via `now_ms()`; `PlayState` unchanged (no timer fields) so phones never see timer
+- Auto-finish: `maybe_auto_finish` called at top of `big_screen/mod_state/game_action/winners/player_page/player_state/player_join/player_answer` handlers (loads quiz, updates `game` in-memory + DB) so any poll/answer after expiry sees `closed`; `game_action` auto-finishes before applying `start/finish/next/end` (finish-after-expiry idempotent); `player_answer` auto-finishes before `status==open` check so late answers rejected (last pick before expiry kept, `elapsed` still `now-opened`)
+- Big screen: `render_big_screen_inner` for `open`+timer adds `<div class=timer id=timer>M:SS</div>` after `q-body` (server `remaining_text` from `opened_at`, so reload shows correct remaining not full); closed/lobby/finished/no-timer show no timer; CSS `.timer` large display font
+- JS (`big_screen.js`): `render(open)` inserts timer div from `st.remaining_text` when `timer_seconds>0`, stores `remainingMs/fetchedAt/questionId` + `fetchState()` immediately + `setInterval(tickTimer,200ms)` for smooth local countdown (`fmtTimer(ceil((remaining-elapsed)/1000))`, updates `#timer` between 250ms polls, `postAction(.../finish)` once per question when `left<=0`); server lazy-close is authoritative (next poll returns `closed`), client POST is backup; `tick` disabled when closed/lobby/finished/no-timer, flags reset per question
+- Export: unchanged (`title/questions/text/active/options/text/correct` only, no timer); import ignores extra keys so timer JSON ignored, new quiz gets 0/0
+- QA labels: exact `Timer minutes`, `Timer seconds`, countdown `M:SS`, `Finish` still visible while open (early finish works), no timer on `/play/*` (body + JSON clean, `play.js` has no timer strings)
